    "html_url": "https://github.com/nelsong6/shows/commit/b50b91be52168c3a9c40605446ce1ad816beb4a0",
    "message": "desktop: gate render pump on new mpv frames (fix ~1GB/hr memory leak)\n\nrender() drove the libmpv GL renderer + Present every 16ms unconditionally,\nre-rendering the same frame ~60x/sec even while paused. Confirmed via live\nmonitoring: private (committed) memory grew a steady ~18 MB/min (~9 GB at 7h\nuptime), CPU-side (GPU memory flat), and kept climbing WHILE PAUSED — i.e.\npump-driven, not decode-driven.\n\nResolve mpv_render_context_update and gate the GL render + Present on\nMPV_RENDER_UPDATE_FRAME (a new frame), or a force_present flag set on\nresize / first paint / standby-resume so the surface is never left stale.\nThe per-tick dcomp.Commit() is kept so the WebView2 overlay still updates and\nfirst paint is not gated out (an earlier naive gate blanked the overlay).\n\nAlso collapses needless 60/sec composition/VRR-path churn while pinned, the\nsuspected driver of the monitor flash.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOS5KECdoAKGI1MGI5MWJlNTIxNjhjM2E5YzQwNjA1NDQ2Y2UxYWQ4MTZiZWI0YTA",
